{"path":"named_req/BasicFormatter","title":"C++ named requirements: BasicFormatter (since C++20)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">C++ named requirements:</span><em class=\"t-named-req\">BasicFormatter</em><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/BasicFormatter","section":"named_req","kind":"page","summary":"BasicFormatter is a type that abstracts formatting operations for a given formatting argument type and character type. Specializations of std::formatter are required to meet the requirements of BasicFormatter.","html":"<p><strong class=\"selflink\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">BasicFormatter</em></strong> is a type that abstracts formatting operations for a given formatting argument type and character type. Specializations of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/format/formatter\">std::formatter</a></span> are required to meet the requirements of <em class=\"t-named-req\">BasicFormatter</em>.\n</p><p>A <em class=\"t-named-req\">BasicFormatter</em> is a <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/Formatter\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">Formatter</em></a> if it is able to format both const and non-const arguments.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Requirements\">Requirements</h3>\n<p>A type satisfies <em class=\"t-named-req\">BasicFormatter</em> if it is semiregular, meaning it satisfies:\n</p>\n<ul><li> <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/DefaultConstructible\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">DefaultConstructible</em></a>\n</li><li> <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/CopyConstructible\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">CopyConstructible</em></a>\n</li><li> <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/CopyAssignable\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">CopyAssignable</em></a>\n</li><li> <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/Destructible\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">Destructible</em></a>\n</li><li> <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/Swappable\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">Swappable</em></a>\n</li></ul>\n<p>And, given the following types and values, the expressions shown in the table below are valid and have the indicated semantics:\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td> Type\n</td>\n<td> Definition\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>CharT</code>\n</td>\n<td> a character type\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>Arg</code>\n</td>\n<td> a formatting argument type\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>Formatter</code>\n</td>\n<td> a <em class=\"t-named-req\">Formatter</em> type for types <code>Arg</code> and <code>CharT</code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>OutputIt</code>\n</td>\n<td> a <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/OutputIterator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">LegacyOutputIterator</em></a> type\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>ParseCtx</code>\n</td>\n<td> <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/format/basic_format_parse_context\"><span class=\"kw3173\">std::<span class=\"me2\">basic_format_parse_context</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>CharT<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>FmtCtx</code>\n</td>\n<td> <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/format/basic_format_context\"><span class=\"kw3176\">std::<span class=\"me2\">basic_format_context</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>OutputIt, CharT<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td> Value\n</td>\n<td> Definition\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code>\n</td>\n<td> a value of type (possibly const-qualified) <code>Formatter</code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">g</span></code>\n</td>\n<td> a value of type <code>Formatter</code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">arg</span></code>\n</td>\n<td> an lvalue of type <code>Arg</code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">t</span></code>\n</td>\n<td> a value of type convertible to (possibly const-qualified) <code>Arg</code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">parse_ctx</span></code>\n</td>\n<td> an lvalue of type <code>ParseCtx</code> satisfying all following conditions:\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">parse_ctx.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> points to the beginning of the <span class=\"t-spar\">format-spec</span> of the replacement field being formatted in the <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/format/basic_format_string#Format_specification\">format string</a>.\n</li><li> If <span class=\"t-spar\">format-spec</span> is not present or empty, then either <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">parse_ctx.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> parse_ctx.<span class=\"me1\">end</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>parse_ctx.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"st0\">'}'</span></span></code>.\n</li></ul>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">fmt_ctx</span></code>\n</td>\n<td> an lvalue of type <code>FmtCtx</code>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tr>\n<th>Expression\n</th>\n<th>Return type\n</th>\n<th>Semantics\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">g.<span class=\"me1\">parse</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>parse_ctx<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code>ParseCtx::iterator</code>&nbsp;\n</td>\n<td>\n<ul><li> In the range <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">parse_ctx.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">parse_ctx.<span class=\"me1\">end</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code><code>)</code></span>, parses the <span class=\"t-spar\">format-spec</span> for type <code>Arg</code> until the first unmatched character.\n</li><li> Throws <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/format/format_error\">std::format_error</a></span> unless the whole range is parsed or the unmatched character is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"br0\">}</span></span></code>. <sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\">[note 1]</a></sup>\n</li><li> Stores the parsed format specifiers in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">g</span></code> and returns an end iterator of the parsed range.\n</li></ul>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f.<span class=\"me1\">format</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>arg, fmt_ctx<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code>FmtCtx::iterator</code>\n</td>\n<td>\n<ul><li> Formats <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">arg</span></code> according to the specifiers stored in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code>, writes the output to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">fmt_ctx.<span class=\"me1\">out</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> and returns an end iterator of the output range.\n</li><li> The output shall only depend on\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">arg</span></code>,\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">fmt_ctx.<span class=\"me1\">locale</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>,\n</li><li> the range <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">parse_ctx.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">parse_ctx.<span class=\"me1\">end</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code><code>)</code></span> from the last call to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f.<span class=\"me1\">parse</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>parse_ctx<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, and\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">fmt_ctx.<span class=\"me1\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>n<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> for any value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">n</span></code> of type <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\">std::size_t</a></span>.\n</li></ul>\n</li></ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">This allows formatters to emit meaningful error messages.</span>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3892\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 3892</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++20\n</td>\n<td>the value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">pc.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> was unclear if <span class=\"t-spar\">format-spec</span> is not present\n</td>\n<td>made clear\n</td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Requirements","id":"Requirements"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"named_req","title":"Named Requirements"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"C++ named requirements: BasicFormatter (since C++20)","children":[{"label":"Requirements","note":"A type satisfies BasicFormatter if it is semiregular, meaning it satisfies:","children":[{"label":"CharT","note":"a character type"},{"label":"Arg","note":"a formatting argument type"},{"label":"Formatter","note":"a Formatter type for types Arg and CharT"},{"label":"OutputIt","note":"a LegacyOutputIterator type"},{"label":"ParseCtx","note":"std::basic_format_parse_context<CharT>"},{"label":"FmtCtx","note":"std::basic_format_context<OutputIt, CharT>"},{"label":"f","note":"a value of type (possibly const-qualified) Formatter"},{"label":"+5 more"}]},{"label":"Defect reports","note":"The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards."}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":348,"codeBlockCount":0}
